getGINAsat.py is designed to feed product files from GINA's NRT source to the AWIPS 
EDEX ingest (default) however, it can also retrieve files for other purposes when used 
with the "-ni" (no ingest) option. It is typically run from cron using the 
"getLatestSat_GINA.sh" wrapper for logging and file locking. If the "-noingest" option
is used, the shell script could be modified to move files from the current working 
directory.


usage: getGINAsat.py [-h] [-a {uaf5,gilmore,uafgina}]
                     [-s {terra,snpp,noaa21,noaa20,metop-c,metop-b,gcom-w,aws}]
                     [-m MATCH]
                     [-l {level1,level2,scmi,mirs_awips,mirs_scmi,sst_awips,nucaps_level2,clavrx_scmi,mirs_level2,awips,NucapsAwips,edr_scmi,sst_geotif,raw,nucaps_level1,mod14,mirs_level2,mirs_geotif_l1,mirs_awips,level1_agg,level0-ipopp,geotiff_polar_l2,geotiff_polar_l1,geotiff_ngfs_l2,geotiff_level2,geotiff_l2,geotiff_l1,geotiff_gm_l2,geotiff_gm_l1,geotiff,FireAwips,fire,edr_geotiff_l1,clavrx_level2,clavrx_geotiff_l1,binary_slice,acspo_level2,,acspo_awips}]
                     [-t] [-ni] [-reg] [-bm BACKMINS] [-v] [-ver]
                     [{viirs,modis,metop,avhrr,atms,amsr2,all}]


### One or more sensor types are required "positional" arguments that are not 
preceeded by an option indicator. Below are the only valid sensor choices:
   viirs
   modis
   avhrr
   atms
   metop
   amsr2
   all

### Below are optional arguments are preceeded by option indicators (either one dash
and a letter, or two dashes and a keyword). Optional arguments are not required unless a 
specific constraint is needed. An option that is not specified indicates any or all 
items in that category.

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -a ANTENNA, --antenna ANTENNA
                        antennas include: {uaf5, gilmore, uafgina}
  -s SATELLITE, --satellite SATELLITE
                        satellites include: {snpp, noaa20, noaa19, noaa18, noaa15, aqua, terra}
  -l LEVEL, --level LEVEL 
			levels include: {level1,level2,scmi,mirs_awips,mirs_scmi,sst_awips,nucaps_level2,clavrx_scmi,mirs_level2,awips,NucapsAwips,edr_scmi,sst_geotif,raw,nucaps_level1,mod14,mirs_level2,mirs_geotif_l1,mirs_awips,level1_agg,level0-ipopp,geotiff_polar_l2,geotiff_polar_l1,geotiff_ngfs_l2,geotiff_level2,geotiff_l2,geotiff_l1,geotiff_gm_l2,geotiff_gm_l1,geotiff,FireAwips,fire,edr_geotiff_l1,clavrx_level2,clavrx_geotiff_l1,binary_slice,acspo_level2,,acspo_awips},
  -m MATCH, --match MATCH
			match substring in filename
  -bm BACKMINS, --backmins BACKMINS
                        num mins back to request products
  -t, --test            use test NRT data stream
  -ni, --noingest
			turns off default to move files to the EDEX ingest directory and 
			leaves them in the current working directory
  -reg, --regionalsat   add the prefix Alaska to regionalsat filenames that
                        AWIPS needs needs for identification
  -v, --verbose         verbose flag
  -ver, --version       report version level

##############################################
getLatestSat_GINA.sh   - a wrapper script for running getGINAsat.py from cron that checks for 
                         multiple instances that might still be running and appends output to an 
                         AWIPS log file.  Arguments are passed through to the python script, so 
			 all arguments listed above apply.
##############################################

Examples:

getGINAsat.py --level awips viirs modis avhrr
       - retrieves any awips formatted viirs, modis, or avhrr data from any platform data within 
	 the default search time of the last 60 mins.
getGINAsat.py --satellite noaa20 --test -bm 85 viirs
       - retrieves any awips formatted viirs data from noaa20 within the specified search time
         of the last 85 mins. 
getGINAsat.py --level mirs_awips --test -bm 75 atms avhrr
       - retrieves any mirs products in awips format from atms or avhrr(AMSU-A/MHS)  within the 
	 specified search time of the last 75 mins. 
getGINAsat.py --level scmi --test -bm 90 viirs modis
       - retrieves any SCMI tile formatted viirs or modis from any platform data within 
	 the specified search time of the last 90 mins.

